wg-newbie-option-show-tag = Show my newbie tag (new players only; turning it off drops newbie protection)
guide-entry-wg-rule-conflict-six-new-players = Conflict Rule 6 - New Players

wg-newbie-welcome-title = Welcome to Wolfgate
wg-newbie-welcome-text = You're new here. Until you've played {$hours} hours, your newbie tag puts a learner plate over your head and [bold](L)[/bold] after your ship's name, and other players are told to go easy on you while it shows.

    - [bold]Ahelp[/bold] (F1) to ask an admin anything. Nobody minds questions.
    - The [bold]guidebook[/bold] (Numpad 0) explains jobs, ships and the rules.
    - Read Conflict Rule 6 to see what other players can and can't do to you.
    - You can hide your tag in Options > Extra, but then the new player rules don't cover you.
wg-newbie-welcome-dont-show = Don't show this again
wg-newbie-welcome-rules = Read the new player rules
wg-newbie-welcome-ok = Got it
wg-newbie-crew-title = Join a crew first
wg-newbie-crew-text = You've only just started. Don't buy your own ship yet: join a crew first.

    Pick a job from the [bold]Crew[/bold] list when you join, or start at a station and ask on the radio for a crew that needs a hand. Captains will show you how things work.
wg-newbie-crew-ok = Okay

